Z||000000||jerpro||02-16-2001||08:32 PM||||I got a @!#^^& sppeding ticket when I was heading back from NH last tuesday. And I feel in a spped trap in NY. I was going 75 in a 65 and the officer wrote me down for 85.<BR>I can't go to court but I have written a letter and I  would appreciate any comments. I have to send the letter tomorro so, pelase help. Thanks<P>Dear Sir or Ma’am,<P>	I have been issued a speeding ticket in you area. I was informed by the officer on duty that my speeding ticket fine was going to be assessed by you.<BR>The reason I am writing this letter is because I believe that the officer on duty may have made an incorrect judgment on the speed of the vehicle I was driving. I do take responsibility for going 70mph to 75mph but I am certain that the vehicle never reached the speed of 85mph for which the officer charged me with. The person that was in the car with me at the time of the offense, also noted that the speeding violation was excessive. <BR>I would fight the case in court but I live in Michigan and the trip and the court fees would cost me a lot of money, which I don’t have. <BR>I am please asking that you take this into consideration as you asses the fine. Thank you.<P>Sincerely yours:<BR>		<BR>Jeremias P. Rigueiro <P>Witness:<P>Adam Nannini<BR>||||reg||1
