Z||000004||c m west||02-16-2001||09:18 PM||||if it goes to court you can do this only if the officer caught you by radar or laser<P> - file for a " Motion of Discovery " - this is a statement from the technician of the officers equipment that every device he or she used to calculate your speed was set within the correct parameters and specifications for that perticular device.<P> Also - was there any cars around you - signals often bounce bwtween vehicles before returning to the equipment to be calculated<P>hope this helps<P>Eric - West Coast Fiero <A HREF="http://www.cwestco.com" TARGET=_blank>www.cwestco.com</A> ||||reg||1
Z||000005||007DOUG||02-16-2001||10:26 PM||||Just bend over and pay it.<P>I hired a lawyer once before to fight a speeding ticket I didn't deserve. It did no good at all. I could have went to the next higher level of court, but why??? It was going to cost me even more. Not only lawyer fees, but also lost time at work.<P>These stupid little hick towns depend on out-of-staters like you and me for revenue. Heck, the "judge" in this particular town was also the mayor. His mind was made-up before I even entered the room. And best of all, the officer never even showed-up for the trial. COME ON!!!!! <P>Seriously, JUST PAY IT, and rack it up as a life expierence!!!!!!<P>------------------<BR>5 Indy pace Cars<BR>84 T-top<BR>86 SE V6 153K (daily)<BR>86 GT red <BR>86 GT Yellow ASAP<BR>86 GT w/4:10 tranny<BR>86 GT 3.4 Pearl White T-top<BR>88 Coupe<BR>88 Formula 5 speed (soon)<BR>2 88 GT's (twins)<P>But......<BR><I>"Time is my most precious and most perishable of all my possessions."</I>||||reg||13
Z||000006||DXR_DAD||02-16-2001||10:27 PM||||CHANGE&gt;&gt;&gt; I am please asking &gt; to I am asking please.<P>I do take responsibility&gt;&gt;&gt;&gt; for breaking the law but only a little bit?????? <P>Not sure about that one?<P>Just my first thought.<BR>DXR_DAD||||reg||3
Z||000007||My7Fieros||02-16-2001||10:48 PM||||Pay the ticket...its not worth fighting.<BR>Raydars dont lie. If he was using a laser radar, forget it. We started using those and I can clock a mouse in the middle of I-40 in rush hour traffic.<BR>If he was using the older style radar (doppler style) than your argument could be for whats called "tracking history checklist" which is a fancy name for "calibrating your radar"..which I rarely did...didnt matter, its like tuning a piano..needs to be done about that often.<BR>Anyway sorry to hear about your ticket, but it happens to everyone from time to time.<BR>DXR DAD is right, you're already admitting to breaking the law..just pay it.||||reg||1
