Z||000018||RNGCRSH||02-18-2001||10:19 AM||||Can you find out weather or not, your state recognizes the trafic laws of the other state.<P>If they do then pay it. If they dont and you dont ever plan on returning there. forget it<P>Statute of limitations is 7 years in most states for any non felony crime.<P>Due to a speed trap I recieved a ticket in CA when I was 20YO I had no money to pay. I later got a leter saying I owed $3600 in fines and court costs, it also said there was a warrant for my arrest. I am 31 now and was jus recently back in CA and was stopped again. The ran my D.L. and it came up clean.<P>I lived in Louisiana at the time and they only recognized the traffic laws of thier ajoining states||||reg||1
Z||000019||ChopTop||02-18-2001||11:45 AM||||Contact the Michigan Secretary of State and find out if MI recognizes NY tickets.  (But don't call Monday, MI state holiday.)  If, they do, and you don't pay, they may issue a bench warrant on you.  If they don't, and you don't plan on going back to NY, then don't pay it.  <BR>Regardless if you pay or dont pay I would still report the police officer for lying.  Some states do track police officer complaints, and if goes into their tracking system.  Silence equals approval.||||reg||1
